Ladybird keeps failed installed directories available for retry, and
revokes a loaded extension when its reload fails. Chromium disables
before reload in ExtensionRegistrar::DoReloadExtension(), and records
failed paths in failed_to_reload_unpacked_extensions_. This matches the
failed-reload behavior. Gecko loads the manifest before activation in
XPIInstall.installTemporaryAddon(), called by AddonWrapper.reload() for
temporary installs. Ladybird deliberately keeps failed entries across
restarts, so the user can fix the directory and reload it, and revokes a
failed reload.

Ladybird prepares an install without persisting it, and grants newly
declared permissions only when the install is confirmed. Chromium
UnpackedInstaller::InstallExtension() grants active permissions without
an unpacked-install confirmation. Ladybird deliberately requires that
confirmation and keeps command-line reload grants unchanged. WebKit
WebExtensionContext::setGrantedPermissions() keeps explicit grants;
WebExtensionController::load() removes a context when loading fails, and
unload() notifies processes without deleting stored data. Ladybird
likewise separates revocation from storage deletion. WebKit leaves
management UI and failed-entry persistence to its embedding application.
